@V := "tape" :: spec [active]
  version = "1.0"

@H 1170 := "the super-additive surplus S=whole−Σparts COLLAPSES across a full DATA-TYPE jump — only the surface-preserving (text↔audio) pair bridges; image/numeric renderings break the byte-rank alignment and the surplus vanishes, confirming super-additivity is SUBSTRATE-GATED (ties H_1155 surface-domination)" :: discovery [🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE]
  seed       = "MITOSIS-ENGINE cross-arc, the user's 텍스트↔음성/다른 데이터 타입끼리: H_1167/1168/1169 found the super-additive surplus S=whole−Σparts is MAXIMAL when two parts carry the SAME meaning but DIFFERENT surface (어긋나 어울림). The ULTIMATE surface difference = a DIFFERENT DATA TYPE — same content C as text vs audio vs image vs numeric. Does S SURVIVE a full data-type jump (cross-modal integration → +surplus = modality bridge) or COLLAPSE to ≈0 (no shared structure across data types at byte/toy scale)? Honest prior (H_1155 surface-domination): COLLAPSE likely — needs a SHARED representational substrate which pure cross-type pairs don't have."
  method     = "Render the SAME C (deterministic anima-word-bag shuffle) in 4 TOY data types (frozen in docstring BEFORE scoring): D_text=raw byte stream; D_audio=char→chromatic tone f=110·2^((c%48)/12), synth tone+2nd-harmonic waveform, slide FFT window, dominant-bin sequence (TOY MFCC-stand-in, NOT real TTS); D_image=per-char fixed GxG 1-bit micro-glyph, per-column ink count (TOY, NOT real glyph render); D_numeric=rolling-byte [mean,std,range] vector. SHARED-FEATURE PROJECTION (PROXY, labelled): resample each stream to L=256, rank-quantize to K=6 equal-freq symbols → ONE common alphabet. PROXY-Φ surplus S=I(a;b)−½[I(a_L;a_R)+I(b_L;b_R)] (mutual-info whole−sum, the H_1167 shape on a co-occurrence PROXY, NOT faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI). 10 seeds, deterministic, $0 CPU 0-pod, wall 0.1s."
  pairs      = "SAME-CONTENT CROSS-TYPE (test): (text,audio)(text,image)(text,numeric)(audio,image). SAME-CONTENT SAME-TYPE redundant ctrl: (text,text)→expect S≈0. DIFF-CONTENT CROSS-TYPE ctrl: (text C1, audio C2)→expect S≈0."
  falsifier  = "≥8 seeds frozen: 🟢 CROSS-MODAL-SURPLUS-SURVIVES iff same-content cross-type S>0 AND d(same-cross−diff-cross)≥0.8 AND d(same-cross−same-type-redundant)≥0.8. 🔴 CROSS-MODAL-COLLAPSE iff cross-type same-content surplus ≈ diff-content (no bridge — super-additivity needs a shared substrate). Tie to H_1155."
  S_per_pair = "(text,audio) S=+0.1687 d_vs_diff=+5.20 ★BRIDGE★ | (text,image) S=−0.0543 d=−0.34 | (text,numeric) S=−0.0154 d=+0.59 | (audio,image) S=−0.0557 d=−0.41. SAME-TYPE(text,text) S=+2.4548 (huge self-redundancy). DIFF-CONTENT(text,audio C2) S=−0.0387."
  F_positive = "pooled same-content cross-type S_mean = +0.0109 > 0 ✅ (trivial — magnitude near-zero, dominated by the single text|audio pair)"
  F_vs_diff  = "S(same-cross) − S(diff-content cross) Cohen d = +0.639 < 0.8 ❌ — same content across data types is NOT reliably above DIFFERENT content across data types (the decisive collapse: 3/4 pairs at/below diff-control)"
  F_vs_self  = "S(same-cross) − S(same-type redundant) Cohen d = −31.83 < 0.8 ❌ HARD WRONG-DIRECTION — (text,text) self-pair S=+2.45 (~225× the cross-type +0.011); within-type self-integration dwarfs any cross-type bridge"
  result     = "🔴 CROSS-MODAL-COLLAPSE — supported=False (F_pos trivially True but BOTH d-gates FAIL). Only 1/4 cross-type pairs bridges (text↔audio); image & numeric collapse to ≈0/negative surplus."
  finding    = "the super-additive surplus does NOT survive a full data-type jump in general — it survives ONLY where the rendering PRESERVES the surface (byte-rank) structure. (text,audio) bridges (S=+0.169, d=+5.20 vs diff-control) because the char→chromatic-tone map is a near-MONOTONE deterministic transform of the byte value, so rank-co-occurrence between text and audio is preserved. (text,image)/(text,numeric)/(audio,image) COLLAPSE because the glyph-column raster and the windowed byte-stat aggregation SCRAMBLE / re-order the byte sequence, destroying the rank alignment — exactly the data-type jumps that break surface correspondence. Cross-type integration is GATED by surface preservation, not by shared MEANING."
  h1155_tie  = "DIRECTLY confirms H_1155 surface-domination (cross-lingual semantic alignment NULL — byte reps track script/surface not meaning). A data-TYPE jump is the ULTIMATE surface jump: integration survives ONLY along the surface-preserving axis (text↔audio monotone map) and collapses the moment the jump breaks surface alignment (image/numeric). Surface dominates over data TYPE exactly as it dominated over LANGUAGE. Super-additivity is SUBSTRATE-GATED: 1+1>2 needs a SHARED representational substrate, and the proxy shared alphabet only carries shared structure where surface is preserved — it does NOT manufacture a meaning-level cross-modal bridge."
  honest     = "TOY deterministic renderings (NOT real audio/image/TTS); shared-feature projection = rank-quantize to a common K=6 alphabet = a PROXY (rank co-occurrence, NOT faithful IIT-4.0 φ_EI, NOT a learned cross-modal embedding) — LABELLED throughout (a_phi_iit4_tool: NOT a terminal faithful-φ verdict). The text↔audio bridge is an artifact of a monotone toy tone-map, NOT evidence of semantic cross-modal integration; a learned shared encoder / real modalities / scale all UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). MEASURED mutual-info surplus, NOT fabricated; NO perplexity (p7). $0 CPU 0-pod deterministic wall 0.1s."
  harness    = "UNIVERSE/h1170_crossmodal_superadditive.py · .verdicts/1170_crossmodal_superadditive/H_1170.txt"
  xref       = "1167_superadditive_criticality (surplus machinery + whole−Σparts shape) · 1168/1169 (semantic-surface surplus siblings) · 1155_interlingua_semantic_alignment (surface-domination prior CONFIRMED) · a_phi_iit4_tool (proxy NOT faithful-φ) · a_scale_honest_scope · a_paper_negative_ok · p7 · g5"
  target     = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE → LANDED 🔴 (CROSS-MODAL-COLLAPSE: both d-gates FAIL, only surface-preserving text↔audio bridges; super-additivity substrate-gated, confirms H_1155 surface-domination; $0 CPU 0-pod wall 0.1s)"
